# Asks a policy for the next chunk of joint-space actions. The caller gathers the
# observation and sends it here; the policy is a pure function of this request and
# holds no robot state across calls, so one running model can serve any caller and
# the same contract fits a model in its own process, on a local GPU, or remote. A
# source that does keep state (a replay cursor, a server-side action queue) resets
# it when new_episode is true.

# Task instruction for language-conditioned policies. Empty for policies that take
# no prompt.
string prompt

# Current joint state, unnormalized. The policy reads the joint ordering from the
# names and applies its own normalization. Cross-chunk continuity is handled via
# previous_action_chunk and frozen_prefix_steps, not by projecting this state forward
# to a future seam; this field is always the state observed now. The reference consumer
# sends the commanded joint group's positions, with the configured gripper joint
# appended last when one is configured; it fills positions only, so populate velocity
# here if your policy conditions on it.
sensor_msgs/JointState robot_state

# One camera image per view the policy expects, paired with image_names so the
# policy can match each image to a trained input. The arrays line up by index.
# These are raw sensor_msgs/Image and each carries its own encoding; the policy
# server owns any resize and normalization and must honor the encoding field (converting
# bgr8 to rgb8 when needed). The reference consumer forwards camera frames as-is without
# converting them.
sensor_msgs/Image[] images
string[] image_names

# True on the first request of a new episode. A policy that holds state across
# calls resets that state here; a stateless policy ignores it. The reference
# consumer sets it true on its first call of a run and false afterward.
bool new_episode

# The unexecuted tail of the previous chunk, in the policy's own action space. The
# caller stores policy_action_chunk from the last response and sends the still-unexecuted
# part back so the policy can keep the new chunk consistent with it. The tail and the new
# chunk start at the same moment, so the two advance together tick for tick; the first
# frozen_prefix_steps of the tail are the motion that executes while inference runs. Empty
# on the first call and for policies without real-time chunking.
std_msgs/Float64MultiArray previous_action_chunk

# Optional. The observation state the previous chunk was anchored to, in the same
# form as robot_state. A delta-action policy re-references its carried
# previous_action_chunk from this state into the current one; an absolute-action policy
# does not need it. Empty for absolute-action policies, on the first call, and whenever
# previous_action_chunk is empty.
sensor_msgs/JointState previous_anchor_state

# How many leading steps of the new chunk overlap motion already committed while this
# inference runs; the policy freezes those steps to the previous chunk. This is the step
# count real-time chunking calls the inference delay. The reference consumer derives it
# from the inference latency it compensates for, and sends zero on the first call.
uint32 frozen_prefix_steps

# How many steps past the frozen prefix the policy keeps the new chunk close to the
# previous one before letting it diverge: the width of real-time chunking's soft-guidance
# region. (This is not the same as the literature's "execution horizon", the number of
# steps executed before re-inference; that is the caller's committed_action_steps.) Zero
# uses the policy's default. The guidance weight and schedule remain policy-server
# configuration; the reference consumer sends its configured guidance_horizon value,
# zero by default, so zero defers to the server's setting.
uint32 guidance_horizon
---
# How the policy answered this request. The caller executes the chunk on CHUNK_PRODUCED, ends the
# run as complete on NO_MORE_ACTIONS, and fails the run on ERROR and on any value it does not
# recognize, so a response left unfilled (UNKNOWN) reads as a failure rather than as a completed run.
# The chunk is read only on CHUNK_PRODUCED and ignored on every other status.
uint8 UNKNOWN=0          # The field's default; no policy sets this.
uint8 CHUNK_PRODUCED=1   # chunk carries the next actions.
uint8 NO_MORE_ACTIONS=2  # This chunk source chose to stop: a replay reached its end, a queue drained.
                         # Return the final actions in a CHUNK_PRODUCED response first, then
                         # NO_MORE_ACTIONS on the following call, or those actions never execute.
uint8 ERROR=3            # No chunk could be produced: the policy or its serving stack failed.
uint8 status

# The end-of-run reason for NO_MORE_ACTIONS, shown to the operator as information; the failure
# reason for ERROR, shown to the operator as the run's failure. Empty for CHUNK_PRODUCED.
string message

# The chunk as absolute joint positions, one point per policy step. The joint names
# give the ordering. Point spacing is set by the caller's configured control period
# (the executor's dt); any time_from_start a policy sets is advisory and is ignored
# by the reference consumer. The caller densifies and collision-checks this before
# sending it to the controller.
trajectory_msgs/JointTrajectory chunk

# The control period in seconds per step the policy was trained at, advisory. The
# caller plays the chunk at its own configured period and does not read this to time
# the chunk, but warns when the two disagree, since a mismatch scales every joint
# velocity. Non-negative: zero when the policy does not report a rate. A negative
# value is a contract violation the caller flags rather than acts on.
float64 native_control_period

# The same chunk in the policy's own action space, with one row per step. Populate
# the layout as two dimensions, steps then action width, so the caller can identify
# the step axis when it returns the unexecuted tail. The caller stores this and
# returns its tail as previous_action_chunk on the next call, without interpreting it.
# Empty for policies without real-time chunking.
std_msgs/Float64MultiArray policy_action_chunk
